# APEX LOGIC — Context Protocol

`CLAUDE.md` at the repo root is the full ruleset. This file mirrors it for Cursor sessions.

**Read by tier — not all at once** (see `CLAUDE.md` §1, DECISION-13):

**Tier 1 — every session:**
1. `memory-bank/ACTIVE_CONTEXT.md` — live state: In Progress markers, Current Status, Open Decisions, newest session block
2. `memory-bank/DECISIONS.md` — the **Index table at the top only** (19 locked decisions)

**Tier 2 — before ANY code change:**
3. `memory-bank/COMPONENT_MAP.md` — what else your change may break
4. The full text of any DECISION entry your change touches

**Tier 3 — on demand only:** `memory-bank/SESSION_LOG.md` (session history), `memory-bank/PROGRESS.md` (build status), `APEX_LOGIC_PLAN.md` (historical plan — contains known-stale status lines; trust disk state over it).

## Non-Negotiable Design Constraints (always enforce)
- `rounded-none` everywhere — `rounded-full` only on status dots, `rounded-sm` is the absolute max elsewhere
- `tabular-nums` on all stacking numeric columns
- `font-mono` (JetBrains Mono) for data/terminal/micro-labels; `font-sans` (Space Grotesk) for headings and plain-English copy — no third family
- Cyan is the only interactive accent — no blue, violet, or new color variables
- `humanIntent-always-visible` — Human Intent never hidden behind a click
- `terminal-continuous-scroll` — Terminal log animates continuously
- `paused-state-must-pulse` — Amber PAUSED badge uses `animate-pulse`
- `plainenglish-before-diff` — Business risk summary always above code diff
- Aesthetic: **Cyberpunk Bloomberg Terminal** — `bg-neutral-950`, thin borders, no shadows/gradients/glass

## Stack (never deviate)
- React 19 + Vite
- Tailwind CSS 4 — CSS-first `@theme` in `src/index.css`. **There is no `tailwind.config.js`; do not add one.**
- Lucide React (icons)
- react-countup (animated counters)
- React Context + useState — client-only by default. **Narrow exception:** DECISION-9 permits a local-only data layer (`scripts/sync-activity-log.mjs`, `scripts/mediator.mjs`, `src/hooks/useLiveLedgerData.js`) in dev. No hosted server, no database engine, no redux/zustand/tanstack-query.

## Cursor's role (CLAUDE.md §11)
In-editor component tweaks with the dev server live — Tailwind class work, visual iteration against `ui-spec.md`. Architecture, cascading changes to `theme.js`/`AppContext.jsx`/`mockLedgerData.json`, and new DECISIONS entries go to Claude on Opus.

- **`src/docs/` is off-limits to every agent.** Report needed changes; don't apply them.
- **Add a session marker** to `memory-bank/ACTIVE_CONTEXT.md` naming yourself (`cursor`) before your first edit; remove it when done. **One writing agent at a time per file** — if another agent's marker claims your file, stop and ask.
- **`npm run build` and `npm run lint` must exit clean** when you finish.

## After completing any task
Append your session block to `memory-bank/SESSION_LOG.md` (newest first), then update only `Current Status` / `Open Decisions` in `memory-bank/ACTIVE_CONTEXT.md` and rotate the previous newest block out. `ACTIVE_CONTEXT.md` carries **one** session block, never a growing stack.
